{"summary":"Inspection of the current tree shows denitrification is already wired through the model: `step_nitrogen_cycle` includes a denitrification phase driven by NO3, DOC, suboxic pore volume, and denitrifier activity; `ProcessParams` and `default.toml` define the denitrification parameter surface and defaults; and nitrogen export is explicitly tracked via `cumulative_n2_export_mg_n` with dedicated denitrification tests. The proposed amendments do not match the present implementation.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-325f0882","decision":"reject","rationale":"`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs` does implement a denitrification stage after nitrification: it computes `suboxic_pore_volume_l`, applies Monod terms for NO3 and DOC, scales by `state.microbe.denitrifier_activity_index`, subtracts nitrate, increments `state.cumulative_n2_export_mg_n`, and returns alkalinity via `DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N`. `crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs` also exposes explicit oxic/suboxic geometry and pore-volume helpers; the denitrifier activity state lives in `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`, not substrate state. The amendment’s core factual claims are therefore incorrect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-a56c3028","decision":"reject","rationale":"The denitrification parameter surface is present in `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs`: `denitrification_vmax_mg_n_per_l_per_hour`, `denitrification_k_no3_mg_n_per_l`, `denitrification_k_doc_mg_c_per_l`, `denitrification_pore_water_mixing_factor`, and `denitrification_activity_maturation_days`, with defaults in both `ProcessParams::default()` and helper default functions. `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` also contains corresponding default values. This amendment does not describe the current code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-4cbac42a","decision":"reject","rationale":"Explicit N2 export accounting is wired through `state.cumulative_n2_export_mg_n`, which is included in `crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs` nitrogen components and therefore in `total_nitrogen_mg`/budget snapshots. That means denitrification is balanced by moving nitrogen into an explicit tracked export pool, not by relying on the open-system action exemption in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs`. There is also dedicated denitrification coverage in `crates/tank_core/tests/denitrification.rs`, including checks that export metrics are recorded and the nitrogen-cycle stage remains budget-balanced. The amendment is inconsistent with the implementation."}]}